# Animated Clip Box — two cards whose Twitter circle springs open to flood the card while pressed (text colour interpolates black→white) and springs back on release.
# What this test covers: a long hold on each card (spring to full radius, text turns white), quick taps that
# release before the expand spring settles (press-out springs to r=30, below the 35 initial radius), a rapid tap
# burst interrupting both springs, holding on the action title row, and the second (orange) card's colours.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/animated-clip-box"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 40000
wait "text" "Explore Demos" 10000
wait "text" "Learn More" 3000
# Hold the blue card long enough for the circle to cover it.
longpress 200 230 1800
wait 1200
# Hold the orange card.
longpress 200 510 1800
wait 1200
# Quick taps: release long before the expand spring settles.
press 76 230
wait 150
press 76 510
wait 1000
# Rapid burst on both cards interrupts expand/collapse springs mid-flight.
press 300 300 --count 8 --interval-ms 90
press 300 580 --count 8 --interval-ms 90
wait 1200
# The action titles are their own pressables (no onPress) inside the card.
press "text=\"Explore Demos\""
wait 300
press "text=\"Learn More\""
wait 300
longpress 90 666 1200
wait 1200
wait "text" "Explore Demos" 3000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 3000
press "label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
